en my first and  second year of masters  yeah so a little bit about how my thesis  was structured  so the first year was really focused on  exploring  different aspects of architecture that  you might be interested in writing your  thesis on  so the first semester  we researched all of the firms  that were participating in the chicago  biennial  we were given like two three firms to  research each person was able to  pick um a couple of the firms that kind  of aligned with their interests  and write a sort of manifesto and  do a little presentation on those firms  and how they aligned  with what you wanted to pursue it was  also  about learning how to represent things  in a more conceptual and theoretical way  and it was kind of  getting an understanding of what a  thesis was  um and then in second year that's when  we  started like the thesis process  and the summer between the first year  and second year that's where you're  supposed to  do all of your research like all the  background research that's supposed to  build a foundation for your thesis  you're looking at your precedence you're  getting the list of all your readings  and like trying to do as much of the  reading as possible  um you're looking at other projects or  other theses  that could relate to yours  you're looking at the possible  sites and yeah like you're basically  doing all the background research  and that's also when it's not really  structured right  you have basically  sort of may june july and august without  too much contact with your supervisors  and so it's really like self-initiated  research  and so i really wanted to create  um some sort of a structure for myself  so that i don't  waste too much time um  you know not working during that time i  was actually  traveling i was in italy and um  it was actually a nice time for me to  just like  read and relax you know chill on the  beach drink some wine  and yeah that's sort of where i did a  lot of my research  you will see that it has